          "character": 49
        }
      },
      "title": "How it all starts on your laptop",
      "description": "**What it is:** the scripts you run with `bun run …` inside `frontend`.\n\n**How it works:** `dev` frees the ports, then runs two things side by side with `concurrently`:\n- `next dev`: the Next.js app with the API inside it (port 3000).\n- `start-agent.cjs`: the Python agent (port 5001, set by that script).\n\nBoth read their secrets from `backend/.env`.\n\n**Why it matters:** one command starts everything you need to chat locally.\n\n**Watch out:** `dev:backend` still starts the old standalone API from `backend/api`. The normal `dev` command doesn't use it any more."
    },
    {
      "directory": "backend/api",
      "title": "A leftover copy",
      "description": "**What it is:** the old standalone API (Hono running on Bun, port 3001).\n\n**How it works:** on Feb 9 this code moved into `frontend/src/server`, and this copy was left behind. Most files are identical. For example, `routes/chat.ts`, `routes/providers.ts`, `middleware/auth.ts` and `db/schema.ts` match line for line.\n\n**Why it matters:** you can skip this folder while learning.\n\n**Watch out:** two copies means a fix in one isn't in the other. If someone asks why it's here, the honest answer is that it was left behind after the move."
    },
